# What ESP-IDF's start-up and this firmware's static initialisers take from the heap
# before the main task exists - every operation, in order (task p11-01).
#
# Recorded from this firmware running in the QEMU of the pinned ESP-IDF image and
# converted by replaying it over the same build: tools/heap_programme.gdb says how, and
# tools/heap_at_start.py --from-record is what wrote this file. Re-record it when
# ESP-IDF, sdkconfig.defaults or a static initialiser of main/ changes.
#
#   alloc <bytes|runner|scratch> <caps>   one heap_caps_* allocation
#   free <n>                              the block operation <n> allocated
#
# `runner` is sizeof(mm::JobRunner) and `scratch` is agent::kKeptScratchBytes, read
# from the ELF of the build being judged: they are the two that change with the build.
# Recorded from a build of version 0.0.0-dev.
